      "content": "Use Case of Background Repetition"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We often use background-repeat: no-repeat; to prevent repetition, but in some cases, repeating backgrounds can be useful."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "For example, repeating a small image, like a geometric pattern or texture, can help you create a continuous background without needing a large image file."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<div>\n2    <h1>Welcome to Programiz!</h1>\n3    <p>Dive into CSS and start turning boring web pages into something that actually looks good.</p>\n4    <h2>Why Learn with Us?</h2>\n5    <ul>\n6        <li>Code in Your Browser!</li>\n7        <li>Create real-world projects.</li>\n8        <li>Get Certified for on-demand skills.</li>\n9    </ul>\n10</div>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "1div {\n2    background-image: url('/images/learn-css/bg3.png');\n3\n4    background-repeat: no-repeat; \n5}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Remove the background-repeat: no-repeat; in the above CSS."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "You'll notice how the repeated image adds a geometric pattern to the background."
    },
